A set \( S \subseteq \Sigma^* \) is defined as sparse if there exists a polynomial \( p : \mathbb{N} \mapsto \mathbb{N} \) such that for each \( n \in \mathbb{N} \), the number of strings of length \( n \) in \( S \) is bounded by \( p(n) \). Mathematically, this is expressed as:

